STEPS: (add gradually)

1. Get Backend app structure ready
2. Setup the database
3. Connect the database
4. Start with User registration




STACK:

Backend: Node.js + FastiFy + TypeScript
Database: SQlite
ORM: Prisma

1. Get Backend app structure ready
	a. Initialize a Node.js project
	use npm init and configure TypeScript.
	: npm init -y

	b. Install dependencies
	Fastify, Prisma, SQLite, and types.
	: npm install fastify
	: npm install -D typescript ts-node nodemon @types/node (typescript → compiler, ts-node → run .ts files directly, nodemon → auto-reload on file changes, @types/node → TypeScript types for Node.js)

	c. Setup TypeScript config
	Configure tsconfig.json for development.
	: npx tsc --init

	d. Setup Prisma
	Initialize Prisma and connect it to SQLite.
	: npm install prisma @prisma/client
	: npm install sqlite3
	: npx prisma init
	: npx prisma migrate dev --name init (when schema is ready)
	: npx prisma generate

	e. Create Fastify app structure
	folders....

	f. app.ts to register routes/plugins.
	Add basic route /ping or /health endpoint to verify the setup.

	f. Environment variables
	.env for database URLs and other secrets.

	g. Verify the setup
	: curl http://localhost:3000/


2. Setup the database

	More dependency:
	npm install @prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3 (Prisma adapter)
	npm install better-sqlite3 (better-sqlite3 driver)

........................CURL  REQUEST .................................

REGISTRATION:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/user/registration \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"userName":"john6","email":"john6@example.com","password":"123456"}'

LOGIN:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/user/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"userName":"john","password":"123456"}'

PROFILE SELF:

curl -X GET "http://localhost:3000/api/user/profile/self?userId=1"


PROFILE ALL:

curl -X GET "http://localhost:3000/api/user/profile/all?pageNo=1&limit=5"


FRIEND REQUEST:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/friendrequest/send \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"senderId":"1", "receiverId":"2"}'


curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/friendrequest/accept \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"senderId":"1", "receiverId":"2"}'


curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/friendrequest/decline \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"senderId":"1", "receiverId":"2"}'


.......................... CURL   END .....................................


docker compose --env-file ./backend/.env --file docker-compose.yml up --build -d


docker compose --env-file ./backend/.env --file docker-compose.yml down


How to run prisma studio inside the container:
docker exec -it transcendence_be sh



